{"title":"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Joe had walked half way from home to school when he realized he was late. He ran the rest of the way to school. He ran 3 times as fast as he walked. Joe took 6 minutes to walk half way to school. How many minutes did it take Joe to get from home to school?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d7878919e2e94374e475f240b501e9471cd2fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 7.3\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 7.7\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8.3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"393\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1218dbfae7805ea5564ac7ee2a892d0a846653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=rt$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the distance, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the rate, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> is the time. The distances he ran and walked are equal, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/2/272e76e9da321f2bbf940df76479f5faef3540c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_rt_r=r_wt_w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/9/f39199d967e800fad78aa85345b72ef1e1e83bb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> is the rate at which he ran, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c16015b525ef1adc657f6307fa815ebf91026c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the time for which he ran, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/b/79b1cd1c90a159e7a45cc45d0a50cd607f332fb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" /> is the rate at which he walked, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f30b92e27271668052e0b3e3cd9392fa436e96a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the time for which he walked. Because he runs three times faster than he walks, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/0/430fab7165c6e6bcd9b77e6a8e6706a5d950fb7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_r=3r_w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />. We want to find the time he ran, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5e80f4b4cbf356ac9cd0aa058f10810f089892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_r = \\frac{r_wt_w}{t_r} = \\frac{(r_w)(6)}{3r_w} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"195\" height=\"41\" /> minutes. He traveled for a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/1/ed1b64f65bd6a8b7ee7c10e649aa0b1f870b9295.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+2=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"120\" height=\"28\" /> minutes.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that it took Joe <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes to walk halfway. If he ran <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times as fast as that, he went <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/922185d0fb364414bb5ae48993f84abc9132fc06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac63 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"37\" /> minutes for the other half (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/a/57a62c6094699400b9db6da4f46a644cfd02ac46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\frac{d}{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"39\" /> and if we multiply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we are essentially dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). Therefore, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/1/47191b694a225675ab225c24a57779c7347ad2c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 2 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> minutes.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>According to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953f29a2b6ad8f2c5d0a2c619a084c4d6896600e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = rt$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, and if we assume the distance from home to school is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mile, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/0/a30d93fcceec465e541a8a5b48f3d20c7dce7521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} = 6r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" />, meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff36b13430d4b7d785e0438f68f706e5bd46c5b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{1}{12}\\text{ mph}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"38\" />. Then, given that he runs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times the speed he walks, he runs at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28c0cbac1687641d5ad1747d8cccfd210c9f91e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{12}\\text{ mph}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3b0037c3e895d0c9fcee9482b9627979bfd1651.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}\\text{ mph}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"53\" height=\"38\" />. Also, note that he only has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> mile left to reach school. Therefore, once again using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/3/953f29a2b6ad8f2c5d0a2c619a084c4d6896600e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = rt$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/e/32e0e03198b83ffc3af6b4341a948d8106612805.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{1}{4}t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/2/6c240b39d84768470be7a72674d0acf93c133e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = 2$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />. Combining the given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes and the deduced <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes, we reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f63fb11c87d69497b0c2a6caa2172e5ceeee3b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{8\\text{ minutes}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"85\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>-N.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 8\">2005 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016211929\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 249/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2270/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 130/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6452/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.997      1 -total\n 57.45%    6.892      1 Template:AMC8_box\n 40.79%    4.893      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11640:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016211929 and revision id 277713. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}